WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.405
Every day has a pulse.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.555
And now, there's more of yours in one place.

3
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.609
Your inbox, right where your day is.

4
00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:19.792
Gmail and Outlook, side by side.

5
00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:26.888
Pulse reads ahead, so you can see what needs a reply, and what's due.

6
00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:33.305
It finds the dates hiding in an email, and puts them in your calendar.

7
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:42.970
Highlight a line, and it becomes a task, or a card on one of your projects.

8
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:53.922
And when it's time to reply, just say what you mean. Pulse writes it. You press send.

9
00:00:55.867 --> 00:00:58.918
Projects, with room to move.

10
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:07.570
Every plan on a board. Add a card, drag it along, and watch it ship.

11
00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:16.216
Each card holds the detail: a checklist, the dates, your notes.

12
00:01:17.333 --> 00:01:23.801
Then step back, and see it all on a timeline, or every card at once.

13
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.812
And if you're not sure what's left, just ask.

14
00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:38.772
Pulse: Three things are in flight on Pulse OS. The week view is up next, and Priya's Q4 deck is due on Friday.

15
00:01:39.867 --> 00:01:44.781
And your calendar, at last, has room to breathe.

16
00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:52.034
The whole month at a glance, with that meeting from your inbox already there.

17
00:01:55.667 --> 00:02:03.273
Your mail, your plans, your days. Finally talking to each other.

18
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:09.248
Pulse OS. Your day, in a heartbeat.
